Subject: Size testfile's read buffer for its largest request
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

testfile asks for up to 1000 bytes (10 x 100) into a 30-byte buffer and
relies on end-of-file to return 0. With SDL 3.4 the read reaches glibc's
fread, which passes the full count to read(2), and Fil-C traps that
unbounded write.

--- a/test/testfile.c
+++ b/test/testfile.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
     SDL_RWops *rwops = NULL;
-    char test_buf[30];
+    char test_buf[1000];
 
     /* Enable standard application logging */
     SDL_LogSetPriority(SDL_LOG_CATEGORY_APPLICATION, SDL_LOG_PRIORITY_INFO);
